{"name":"Electric Lettuce","hex":"#7bd181","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric.\n An electric car, locomotive, train etc.\n\nAn electric toothbrush.\n\nAn electric typewriter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"lettuce","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible plant, Lactuca sativa and its close relatives, having a head of green or purple leaves.","The leaves of the lettuce plant, eaten as a vegetable; as a dish often mixed with other ingredients, dressing etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lettuce"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electricity","blocks":[{"text":"Electricity is the set of physical phenomena associated with the presence and motion of matter possessing an electric charge. Electricity is related to magnetism, both being part of the phenomenon of electromagnetism, as described by Maxwell's equations. Common phenomena are related to electricity, including lightning, static electricity, electric heating, electric discharges and many others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg/330px-London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electricity"},{"title":"Lettuce","blocks":[{"text":"Lettuce is an annual plant of the family Asteraceae mostly grown as a leaf vegetable. The leaves are most often used raw in green salads, although lettuce is also seen in other kinds of food, such as sandwiches, wraps and soups; it can also be grilled. Its stem and seeds are sometimes used; celtuce is one variety grown for its stems, which are eaten either raw or cooked. In addition to its main use as a leafy green, it has also gathered religious and medicinal significance over centuries of human consumption. Europe and North America originally dominated the market for lettuce, but by the late 20th century the consumption of lettuce had spread throughout the world. In 2023, world production of lettuce was 28 million tonnes, led by China with 53% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Iceberg_lettuce_in_SB.jpg/330px-Iceberg_lettuce_in_SB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lettuce"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Thales.jpg/330px-Thales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Thales.jpg/330px-Thales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A fictional portrait of Thales, the earliest known researcher into electricity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThales.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg/500px-Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg/1280px-Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg/500px-Franklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Benjamin Franklin conducted extensive research on electricity in the 18th century, as documented by Joseph Priestley (1767) History and Present Status of Electricity, with whom Franklin carried on extended correspondence.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFranklin-Benjamin-LOC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/M_Faraday_Th_Phillips_oil_1842.jpg/500px-M_Faraday_Th_Phillips_oil_1842.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/M_Faraday_Th_Phillips_oil_1842.jpg/500px-M_Faraday_Th_Phillips_oil_1842.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Michael Faraday's discoveries formed the foundation of electric motor technology.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM_Faraday_Th_Phillips_oil_1842.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Lichtbogen_3000_Volt.jpg/500px-Lichtbogen_3000_Volt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Lichtbogen_3000_Volt.jpg/500px-Lichtbogen_3000_Volt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An electric arc provides an energetic demonstration of electric current.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALichtbogen_3000_Volt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Panasonic-oxyride.jpg/500px-Panasonic-oxyride.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Panasonic-oxyride.jpg/500px-Panasonic-oxyride.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pair of AA cells. The + sign indicates the polarity of the potential difference between the battery terminals.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanasonic-oxyride.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Electric_motor_cycle_3.png/500px-Electric_motor_cycle_3.png?utm_source=e